      "llm_score": 3,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "Checked the 10 plan items. Most facts match the tree and loc_001. Two claims are overstated. The military item says the Civil War Soldiers Index records \"always record age and birthplace\", but that index card gives only name, side, regiment and rank. Age and birthplace come from the service file, and the father is rarely named before WWI. The marriage item says the parents likely married in Ireland before 1845, yet it searches only Pennsylvania collections for 1830–1848. These are not invented sources, but the claims go beyond what the records give."
