      "llm_score": 3,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "Checked the 11 items. The naturalization item says declarations and petitions before the late 1870s \"often named the petitioner's wife and minor children\". That is not right: pre-1906 naturalization papers usually name only the applicant, and family details became standard after 1906. The death item also says a certificate \"must exist\" because registration began in 1906. Compliance was not complete in the first years, so \"should exist\" is the safer claim. The rest matches the tree and loc_001."
